        "narrative_words": 257,
        "narrative": "The account received regular monthly credits of Rs.236,000 via SWIFT from Gulf Digital Solutions LLC, Dubai, UAE, on 2026-04-30, 2026-05-29, 2026-06-30, 2026-07-31, and 2026-08-31, with a slightly increased amount of Rs.238,000 on 2026-08-31 and 2026-09-30. These credits are consistent with the customer's declared income as a software engineer. However, the pattern of regular debits of Rs.85,000 to a housing finance company for a home loan account on 2026-06-01, 2026-07-01, and 2026-08-03, and a larger debit of Rs.400,000 to a term deposit in the customer's own name on 2026-09-02, raises questions about the source and purpose of these funds.\n\nThe transaction history (POE-003) shows a consistent pattern of credits and debits since 2026-04-30, with a regular monthly frequency (POE-008) and large credit amounts (POE-009), including the initial credit of Rs.236,000 on 2026-04-30. The transactions also involve a counterparty in the UAE (POE-011), which is consistent with the customer's profile as an NRI resident in the UAE.\n\nThe record does not rule out the possibility that the customer is using their income to service their home loan and make investments. However, the large credit amounts and the fact that the customer's declared income is approximately Rs.2.4L per month, which is close to the monthly credit amounts, contradicts the explanation that the credits are solely from the customer's employment income.\n\nThe RFI-006 alert signal has been triggered, indicating a potential red-flag indicator. The statutory basis for this report is Section 12(1)(b) of the Prevention of Money Laundering Act (PMLA), which requires reporting of transactions that may involve proceeds of crime.",
